8. Phase 6 — Telegram CAPTCHA handoff (SIMPLE mode v1)
8.1. Trigger: wrapper exits 2 OR any MCP flow's take_snapshot/take_screenshot shows a gate. Orchestrator (Hermes, never the subagent directly) owns the handoff.

8.2. What Hermes sends to Telegram DM 6583879337 (via the already-connected gateway; keep message <1000 chars, screenshot as attachment):

🧩 CAPTCHA needs you (Hermes browser)
Site: <captcha_url>
Session: <sessionId> (kept open 15 min)
Task: <one-line goal>
1) On your phone open the Site link and solve the check
   (same Wi-Fi/account helps; stay in the same site).
2) Reply here: solved  (or failed <what you saw>)
Screenshot of what I see is attached.
Screenshot source: MCP take_screenshot({sessionId}) (base64 PNG → file → attach) or wrapper log_path sibling PNG. NEVER paste passwords/2FA/cards into this chat.

8.3. Resume logic (on solved):

MCP path: wait_for({sessionId, timeout:15000}) → take_snapshot → if gate gone: continue original steps; else retry navigate({sessionId, url: original}) once → re-check.
browser-use path: re-run SAME task with --cdp (fresh agent, persistent Fortress profile/cookies carry the solved state); if save_browser_state({sessionId, name:"<site>"}) was taken post-solve, load_browser_state first on subsequent runs.
On failed …: report captcha_url + screenshot + user note, back off 10 min, offer: retry later / save state / switch to TAKEOVER (P2).
Timeouts: keep session open ≥15 min during handoff; close_browser_session ONLY after success/fail declared; reaper MAX_IDLE_HOURS=24 must not reap mid-handoff (15 min ≪ 24 h — safe).
8.4. Polling for P2 takeover (implement in P2 only): request_human_takeover → send url (TTL default 5 min, max 30) → poll await_human_takeover({token, timeout:4000}) in a loop (short polls, NOT one long await — MCP client timeouts) → continue. First browser to open claims via HttpOnly cookie.

